# Real HTTP redirects for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. Astro's static build
# also emits meta-refresh stubs for these paths as a fallback for hosts that
# ignore this file, but a server-side redirect is what search engines prefer,
# and it is instant for visitors.
#
# Format: [source] [destination] [code]. The default code is 302, so a
# permanent redirect has to say 301. Sources are matched literally, hence both
# slash variants.
#
# www is NOT handled here. Cloudflare Pages only matches a source path, never a
# hostname (its docs list domain-level redirects as unsupported), so a rule like
# "https://www.rootsoftomorrow.org/* ..." is silently ignored. The www to apex
# 301 is a Cloudflare Redirect Rule instead; see "Canonical hostname" in
# README.md for the exact rule. Don't try to re-add it to this file.

# /about was published and then pulled. Temporary on purpose, same reasoning as
# the parked routes below.
/about         /           302
/about/        /           302

# /chapters is the plural people type for the chapter page. Permanent.
/chapters      /chapter/   301
/chapters/     /chapter/   301

# The Planting Log and Past Events pages are parked, not retired: they are
# expected back once the event tree counts are reconciled. Temporary (302) on
# purpose, so search engines do not fold these URLs into the home page.
/past-events   /           302
/past-events/  /           302
/log           /           302
/log/          /           302
/past-events/* /           302
/past          /           302
/past/         /           302

# URLs from the old Framer site. Google indexed these and outside articles
# link to some of them, so each goes to its closest page here with a 301,
# which passes the old URL's standing on to the new one. The event detail
# pages fall under the parked /past-events/* rule above.
